	```
}

// Whether the most recent pump saw a right-mouse-down (the same record
// FrameEvents.click reports as 2). Read by Container.take_right_click —
// the on_right_click drain (docs/HANDLERS.md). The pump stamps the kind
// on EVERY call — a quiet pump stamps 0 — so the edge expires with the
// frame: the drains see it exactly in the handle_events pass that follows
// the pump, and no clearing handshake is needed. The record is
// window-level (one per process, like click_x/click_y): every registered
// arm sees the edge (broadcast), and the HANDLER disambiguates — read the
// click through the dispatch window (win.click_x()/click_y()), translate
// for scrollables (content_click), hit-test children (contains).
pub func nomen_window_had_right_click = (out bool) {
	```
	#arch: c
	#platform: macos
	// One definition lives in process_events' file-scope block (this file);
	// the extern keeps this function's TU-independent (split builds).
	extern int nomen_last_click_kind;
	return nomen_last_click_kind == 2;
	```
	```
	#arch: aarch64_use_c
	#platform: macos
